# RadarPro root .gitignore
# License: Apache-2.0 (provisional, see LICENSE and Agent Context/reference/RELEASE_AND_GOVERNANCE.md)

### Rust ###
# Build artifacts from the Cargo workspace (crates/*, apps/radar-cli).
/target
**/target

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored. apps/radar-cli is a binary
# crate, so the lockfile is tracked for reproducible builds across the
# workspace.

# Backup files generated by some editors/rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

### wasm-bindgen build output ###
# Regenerated from crates/radar-web's wasm32 build via `wasm-bindgen`; see
# crates/radar-web/README.md for the exact build command. Not hand-written
# source, and the compiled .wasm binary is a large, frequently-changing
# build artifact -- same reasoning as ignoring /target.
**/www/pkg/

### Node / Vite (apps/web) ###
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.vite/
**/.vite/
*.local

# npm/yarn/pnpm debug logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# NOTE: package-lock.json is intentionally NOT ignored; it will be tracked
# once apps/web dependencies are installed.

### Fixtures / large local data ###
# Do not ignore fixtures/ contents by default; large binary radar volumes
# should be added deliberately and documented, not silently excluded here.

### Editors / IDEs ###
.idea/

# VS Code: ignore user-specific workspace state but allow shared,
# repo-recommended settings to be tracked deliberately.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

*.swp
*.swo
*~

### OS cruft ###
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

### Env / secrets ###
# Never commit local environment/credential files.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

### Agent planning context ###
# Local-only stage/architecture planning package; not part of the shipped
# repository.
/Agent Context/
